# Chapter 1: The Bridge Deal. The opening scene is the spec §11.2 example.

=== ch01_intro ===
@bg bridge_dusk
@music tension_low
@sfx gulls
@show TELLEN left smirk
@show SABLE right neutral

TELLEN (smirk): Gentlemen. You look like men who appreciate a fair price.
SABLE (annoyed): He says that to everyone.
@item stolen_crate
GID: That crate's ours.
@hide_item

@choice
- "Name your price." -> pay
- "Walk away." -> walk

@label pay
@set paid_toll = true
TELLEN: Consider it an investment.
@goto end

@label walk
@if paid_toll -> end
TELLEN (neutral): Another time, then.

@label end
@end

=== ch01_ambush ===
@show GID center angry
GID (angry): Walked away, did we? Now the toll-men are coming across.
SABLE: Hold the riverbank. Let them come to us.
@end

=== ch01_camp_chest ===
@show TELLEN center happy
@item stolen_crate
TELLEN (happy): Our crate. And whatever else they stole on top of it.
@hide_item
@end

=== ch01_village ===
@show SABLE center neutral
FERRYMAN: You're the ones taking on the toll-men? Take these. And don't tell them where you got them.
@end

=== ch01_reinforcements ===
@show SABLE center surprised
SABLE (surprised): Riders on the north road. They're sending more.
@end

=== ch01_captain ===
@show TELLEN left neutral
@show CAPTAIN right angry
CAPTAIN (angry): Nobody crosses without paying.
TELLEN (smirk): We crossed. Now we're collecting.
@end

=== ch01_outro ===
@show TELLEN left smirk
@show GID right happy
GID (happy): Gate's ours. Crate's ours.
TELLEN (smirk): And the toll is ours, too. I told you. A fair price.
@end
